Z||000002||theogre||05-20-2001||01:26 PM||||The list of things changed/fixed on the DIS version is very extensive.... I've been working on a big update of the 4 cylinder QRG. I still have some things I need to inspect at a scrap yard to verify some data. That's going to be awhile....<P>In short,,, The DIS motor should really be considered a Third, completely diferant, engine system from the distributor L4 and the V6.<P>One thing I've noticed is that it appears GM unified all the cast iron to get inventory down. In otherwords they have made the same iron fit both S10 inline and FWD systems. The S10 I got a quick look at even had starter holes punched in it. I'll have to find one in a scrap yard this summer and really go over it good.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||05-21-2001||10:57 AM||||Yeah, it's hard to beat a DIS Duke for reliability.  But I'd like to try having a "scary" Fiero for a change with about 175 hp.||||reg||12
